<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Limerick</h1><p class="st-meta">922 CE – 977 CE (approx.) · capital Limerick</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Norse town-kingdom on the Shannon estuary whose fall to the Dal Cais opened the way for Brian Boru's rise.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> had raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a> since the 9th century, and in 922 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomrair-mac-ailchi">Tomrair mac Ailchi</a> established a permanent fleet base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>, Hlymrekr. The settlement competed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dublin">Kingdom of Dublin</a> for control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-sea">Irish Sea</a> trade and raided deep into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Connacht</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> was a fortified trading port on an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a>, dealing in slaves and plunder. Its kings were rivals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>'s dynasty, losing a war with them in 937. In the 960s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivar-of-limerick">Ivar of Limerick</a> allied with Irish kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a> against the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dal Cais</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mathgamain-mac-cennetig">Mathgamain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-cais">Dal Cais</a> defeated the Norse at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sulcoit">Sulcoit</a> in 967 and sacked the town. Brian killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivar-of-limerick">Ivar</a> and his sons on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scattery-island">Scattery Island</a> in 977. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a> became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty">O'Brien</a> capital and later the seat of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-thomond">Kingdom of Thomond</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 922 CE – 977 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.05%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>922 CE – 977 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Limerick</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Tomrair mac Ailchi, Ivar of Limerick</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Norse Limerick, Hlymrekr</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=950&amp;focus=kingdom-of-limerick" aria-label="Kingdom of Limerick on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4487 362 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Limerick lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4807 618L4823 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4807 618h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4807 618h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Limerick. <a href="/atlas?year=950&amp;focus=kingdom-of-limerick">On th